deep.reconstruction:
There is no mathematics on this page. Folio 84v is the blank back of the Wöhler letter dated Göttingen, 26 March 1875 (the previous page, 84r). The faint brown writing is ink bleeding through from the front, so it appears mirror-reversed. The layout matches 84r line for line:
- the date line at top right;
- the centred salutation 'Hochzuverehrender Herr Professor.';
- a first paragraph of about 11 lines, including the overlong line 'des Sciences. Ich habe ihm bereits dafür gedankt…', which sticks out to the left in mirror image;
- the small interlinear insertion '{+sende+}', which shows mirrored at the upper left;
- a second paragraph of about 5 lines ('Nachdem Sie davon Gebrauch gemacht haben…');
- two closing lines ('Mit der Bitte, mir den Empfang des Manuscr. anzeigen zu wollen');
- the closing 'Hochachtungsvoll / Ihr ganz ergebenster / Wöhler.'

Historical context: Wöhler is forwarding to Heinrich Weber the original of Riemann's 1861 Paris prize memoir on heat conduction (the 'Commentatio mathematica, qua respondere tentatur quaestioni ab Ill.ma Academia Parisiensi propositae'). The Académie des Sciences had lent it, by a concession from J.-B. Dumas, for Weber's edition of Riemann's Gesammelte Werke (1876). Weber's acknowledgement of 31 March 1875 is the next page (85r). The page contains no derivations, formulas or mathematical content to reconstruct.
